wrote /work/canada/sweep/inspect/rings.json: 25 TE rings, 380 control rings
The trailing-edge rings are not distorted cells: every ring keeps sJ >= 0.85 (mesh mean 0.95) and none of the 10 inverted cells lies in the trailing-edge region x > 9.0 - they sit at least 3.57 upstream. The raggedness is geometric: around a ring the axial (x) station wobbles by up to 0.292 (median 0.087) and the in-plane spline deviation reaches 0.220; the kink angle along the ring polylines reaches 136 deg (p90 median 96 deg). The rings are nested around the tip with a mean spacing of 0.089 that jumps by up to 0.352 between neighbours, so the median ring wobble is 1.6x its own spacing. The mid-channel control rings wobble by a comparable amount (median 0.095) with smaller kinks (p90 median 77 deg) and a far finer spacing (jump median 0.009), so normalised by the spacing the control rings are ragged too (8.4x). The correlation between ring wobble and the ring's worst scaled Jacobian is -0.65 over the TE rings: the more ragged rings touch slightly lower-sJ cells, but never inverted ones - the raggedness is a property of the post-processed vertex columns, not of bad cells.
